# Math Utilities

A small collection of integer math functions for use in other programs.
These implement common numerical algorithms suitable for systems without
floating-point hardware.

## Absolute Value

Returns the absolute value of an integer, defined as:

$$|n| = \begin{cases} n & \text{if } n \geq 0 \\ -n & \text{if } n < 0 \end{cases}$$

    abs(n: int) -> int
        if n < 0 then return -n
        n

## Power

Computes $b^e$ for non-negative exponent $e$ using repeated multiplication.
The time complexity is $O(e)$ — a future version could use
**exponentiation by squaring** to achieve $O(\log e)$.

> **Note:** Only non-negative exponents are supported. Passing a negative
> exponent will return 1 (the loop body never executes).

    power(base: int, exp: int) -> int
        var result: int = 1
        for i = 0; i < exp; i++
            result = result * base
        result

## Greatest Common Divisor

Uses the [Euclidean algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euclidean_algorithm)
to find $\gcd(a, b)$. The algorithm relies on the identity:

$$\gcd(a, b) = \gcd(b, \; a \bmod b)$$

repeatedly replacing the larger operand until the remainder is zero.

| Step | $x$ | $y$ |
|------|-----|-----|
| 0    | 48  | 18  |
| 1    | 18  | 12  |
| 2    | 12  | 6   |
| 3    | 6   | 0   |

    gcd(a: int, b: int) -> int
        var x: int = abs(a)
        var y: int = abs(b)
        while y != 0
            t = y
            y = x % y
            x = t
        x
